        "answer": {
          "short": "$u=3x$, $u'=3$; $v=x+5$, $v'=1$; $y'=\\dfrac{15}{(x+5)^2}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}u&=3x,&u'&=3\\\\v&=x+5,&v'&=1\\\\y'&=\\frac{u'v-uv'}{v^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{3(x+5)-3x(1)}{(x+5)^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{3x+15-3x}{(x+5)^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{15}{(x+5)^2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
