        "answer": {
          "short": "$u=x^3$, $u'=3x^2$; $v=x^2-4$, $v'=2x$; $y'=\\dfrac{x^2(x^2-12)}{(x^2-4)^2}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}u&=x^3,&u'&=3x^2\\\\v&=x^2-4,&v'&=2x\\\\y'&=\\frac{u'v-uv'}{v^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{3x^2(x^2-4)-x^3(2x)}{(x^2-4)^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{3x^4-12x^2-2x^4}{(x^2-4)^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{x^4-12x^2}{(x^2-4)^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{x^2(x^2-12)}{(x^2-4)^2}\\end{align*}$$",
